  "varnames": [],
  "consts": [
   "core/parsers/bass_pro_ack.py - Bass Pro Shops Order Acknowledgement.\n\nSource: INTERNATIONAL DIRECT GROUP INC -> BASS PRO SHOPS. Each ``Order #`` is\none delivery entity (Ctrl # groups several). The item block is a colour x size\nmatrix printed as a SKU line followed by a ``Size >`` header row and a ``Qty >``\nrow - there is NO TOTAL column, so sizes/quantities are positionally aligned:\n\n    Ctrl # 707036 Status : OPEN Date 06/11/26 Terms: BP 2% NET 60\n    Order # 14579877 Dept: I24\n    SKU/Cust Style Whse Ln Status Retail Price Qty SP Extension\n    2807P MDW MEDIUM WASH DRIFTWOOD CROP 04 1 OPEN 0.00 1,512\n    Size > 2 4 6 8 10 12 14 16 18\n    Qty > 120 132 192 204 240 228 168 120 108\n    199382050427 ... (per-size UPC, ignored)\n\nWhse (2-4 cap token, e.g. ``MDW``) is the colour CODE; the human-readable colour\nname (``MEDIUM WASH``) is the leading words of the description before the product\n(``DRIFTWOOD CROP``). The SKU-line qty (1,512) equals the sum of the ``Qty >``\nrow, so it is captured as ``printed_row_total`` for cross-checking.\n\nThe text layer sometimes GLUES the Whse code to the colour name (``MDWMEDIUM``\ninstead of ``MDW MEDIUM``) - this parser recovers the split using the warehouse\ncode length learned from the clean (space-separated) SKU lines.\n\nThe per-SKU style (``2807P`` vs ``2807P27``) is a style+season code, NOT a\nper-colour style, so every line in an order is normalised to the base style\n(stripping the 2-digit season suffix) - this keeps ``consolidate_entities_``\nfrom over-splitting one Order # into several entities.\n",
   0,
   [
    "annotations"
   ],
   null,
   [
    "Counter"
   ],
